  "body": "Direct-PR: dev-swift has been red since #400 (d92775e); this two-line test fix unblocks every PR, including #405 and #433.\nClaim: cloud/orch\n\n**Problem.** `HFRKit tests (Linux)` fails on `TopicPageFlagOracleTests.listsCoverTheOracles` (\"Every topic oracle of LOT-003 and LOT-003-flag is in exactly one list\", line 96).\n\n**Cause.** The two PRs landed in this order:\n- #332 added the check that every topic oracle sits in exactly one list.\n- #400 then added two new LOT-003 oracles, `R96c` and `R96d`: a deleted private conversation, seen by its owner and by its recipient (#169). Neither PR saw the other.\n\n**Change.** Both pages carry no `delflag` and no `nonlu` link, and legacy's `isFavoritesOrRead` is `\"\"`. So they go in `noLink`, next to `RA5` (also a deleted conversation). The doc comment now says \"deleted conversations\". Nothing else changes.\n\n**Tests.** `swift test --filter \"TopicPageFlagOracleTests|TopicPageMetadataOracleTests\"` passes locally on Linux:\n- `listsCoverTheOracles` is green again.\n- `noLinkNoFlag` now runs on R96c and R96d and passes, so the new list entries are checked against the raw pages, not only listed.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CJf1S2KuydxQwVejJK)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Updated topic-page test fixtures to include `R96c` and `R96d` among conversations without links.\n  * Adjusted the fixture description to refer to deleted conversations in the plural. These changes affect test coverage and wording; no user-facing behavior changes are included in this update.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
